{"id": "EUVD-2026-86221", "enisaUuid": "eaa00441-6b86-3baa-a658-0966bc06f903", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: L2CAP: validate connectionless PSM length\n\nConnectionless L2CAP frames carry a two-byte PSM at the start of the\npayload.  l2cap_recv_frame() currently reads that PSM unconditionally\nafter validating only the outer L2CAP length.\n\nA malformed connectionless frame with a zero- or one-byte payload can\ntherefore make the parser read beyond the advertised skb payload and use\ntailroom bytes as part of the PSM.  A VHCI-backed QEMU reproducer\ninjected a one-byte connectionless payload and reached the unchecked\nread.\n\nReject connectionless frames that cannot contain the PSM before reading\nor pulling it.  This preserves all valid connectionless frames while\ndropping only structurally incomplete packets.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:03:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:58:02", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8104cd9859b6de0826cffa68adf2c1461185823b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9448e6f693fcf1f0ac4ee648a9b2cc83bfe4a982", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22fc1ce4e37c81d4e7aac01566ebdc232214540d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/72e26293a231f63a856340d3a1f0f5fc29bf87e5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3502ede8aed3c3ee1786d952a11054ac737d1a38", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ae69dca122f6d6046a68cf40153e6e827c77ff5c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a40a5f922546b3bd7c094d882b29177db4f2abe0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97408", "GHSA-39rm-4xq5-hvr6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "334c339d-e968-3929-a8df-04d249168aeb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <72e26293a231f63a856340d3a1f0f5fc29bf87e5"}, {"id": "40802a45-4934-3c2e-bbaa-562804e9fdff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "45b67a8e-dd63-3687-aacd-d170fb93aea0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "63fd733c-4e8b-3988-9448-e635274fe93c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "64d68c27-a143-3786-b3a4-a96aa73e18c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "76c5b301-47f5-395e-8d23-895f9275e665", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <8104cd9859b6de0826cffa68adf2c1461185823b"}, {"id": "7e241a30-450b-3e9a-89be-99b762c74548", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <3502ede8aed3c3ee1786d952a11054ac737d1a38"}, {"id": "7ea879e7-af5b-30f1-ad63-0ba86676ca4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "9239570a-199a-3505-b3c3-bccb23b4b108", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <a40a5f922546b3bd7c094d882b29177db4f2abe0"}, {"id": "a332271d-24de-3fa9-b6bf-a058f6fe9dc5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <ae69dca122f6d6046a68cf40153e6e827c77ff5c"}, {"id": "a7fcf640-7ee1-38dc-b956-613cd357be2d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "b23624ea-160b-3772-b7c4-be0b10551c46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <9448e6f693fcf1f0ac4ee648a9b2cc83bfe4a982"}, {"id": "cc4957cd-4685-36c6-ae77-52738121bbed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <22fc1ce4e37c81d4e7aac01566ebdc232214540d"}, {"id": "f41dc81b-8242